  "outlook": "\u201cAs we look ahead to 2021, we are encouraged by conditions in our end markets, the ongoing execution against our strategic initiatives, and the improvement in order trends that we have seen during the fourth quarter and so far this year,\u201d noted Sherman. \u201cWe are also closely monitoring the potential for economic stimulus and increased investment in U.S. infrastructure under the new administration, and have positioned ourselves to be prepared for further recovery in market conditions. With this momentum, we are expecting a strong 2021, with top-line growth, double-digit improvement in pre-tax earnings, and adjusted EPS* of between $1.73 and $1.85.\u201d"
